      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1752168148521,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design Uber ",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design Uber ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "p2LTz1agKGkPce1IR8wVt",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 13155.380765594633,
      "y": -987.9100001254409,
      "width": 856.4793701171875,
      "height": 2225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJQ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 868573750,
      "version": 2422,
      "versionNonce": 1021352502,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1752198390929,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional Requirements: \n    - User request ride with start and end location.\n    - You get rough idea about pricing for different vehicle \n    - and then you choose vehicle and start ride by searching driver.\n    - once drive accept, \n    - you redirect to trip page to have live state of location \n        and about trip details. \n    - finish trip and paid rupees. \n\n    \nNon functional requiremetns\n    - High scalable and availability\n    - consistency of ride, not two driver used single ride. \n    - alerts and montoring\n    - Low latency\n\n\nEstimations: \n    - 1B total users. \n    - 100M DAU. \n    - try for avg 2 ride per day\n    - 200M ride per day avg->\n    - ride creation -> 4000 ride per second.\n    - peak -> 100k ride at same time.\n    - Driver location update -> send every 5 seconds. \n\nEntities: \n    - user, userprofile, ride, trip, tripReceipt, payment, vehicle\n\n\nApi Design: \n\n-  search the availability by putting source and esitnation\n\n api/v1/search/?source=\"\" &&destimation=\"\". GET\n \n Response: [\n  options: [\n   {\n       vehicle1, price ,time\n   },\n      {\n       vehicle2, price, time\n   }\n ....\n ]\n\n\n- for request creation for particular vehicle.\n\n/api/v1/ride/         POST\n\nRequest: {\n  source, \n  destination\n  vehicle.\n}\n\nResponse: {\n  RideId: <>\n}\n\nClient can poll for checking any driver found\nand backend will send notification to driver \n\n\n- accept / deny ride request by driver. \n\n/api/v1/ride/accept?rideid=<>    PUT\n\nResponse: {\n   tripdetails: {tripDetail}\n}\n\nand client redirect to trip details page. \n\n\n- websocket connection with trip management\n    service\n\n\nws:/api/trip/{tripID}. ->  ( basically first it will send https -> upgraded to websocket. \n                                   with send the headers require for websocket conversion. )\n\n \n\n- api for trip completion.\n\nafter that it will redirect to payment page -> see payment system design.    ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional Requirements: \n    - User request ride with start and end location.\n    - You get rough idea about pricing for different vehicle \n    - and then you choose vehicle and start ride by searching driver.\n    - once drive accept, \n    - you redirect to trip page to have live state of location \n        and about trip details. \n    - finish trip and paid rupees. \n\n    \nNon functional requiremetns\n    - High scalable and availability\n    - consistency of ride, not two driver used single ride. \n    - alerts and montoring\n    - Low latency\n\n\nEstimations: \n    - 1B total users. \n    - 100M DAU. \n    - try for avg 2 ride per day\n    - 200M ride per day avg->\n    - ride creation -> 4000 ride per second.\n    - peak -> 100k ride at same time.\n    - Driver location update -> send every 5 seconds. \n\nEntities: \n    - user, userprofile, ride, trip, tripReceipt, payment, vehicle\n\n\nApi Design: \n\n-  search the availability by putting source and esitnation\n\n api/v1/search/?source=\"\" &&destimation=\"\". GET\n \n Response: [\n  options: [\n   {\n       vehicle1, price ,time\n   },\n      {\n       vehicle2, price, time\n   }\n ....\n ]\n\n\n- for request creation for particular vehicle.\n\n/api/v1/ride/         POST\n\nRequest: {\n  source, \n  destination\n  vehicle.\n}\n\nResponse: {\n  RideId: <>\n}\n\nClient can poll for checking any driver found\nand backend will send notification to driver \n\n\n- accept / deny ride request by driver. \n\n/api/v1/ride/accept?rideid=<>    PUT\n\nResponse: {\n   tripdetails: {tripDetail}\n}\n\nand client redirect to trip details page. \n\n\n- websocket connection with trip management\n    service\n\n\nws:/api/trip/{tripID}. ->  ( basically first it will send https -> upgraded to websocket. \n                                   with send the headers require for websocket conversion. )\n\n \n\n- api for trip completion.\n\nafter that it will redirect to payment page -> see payment system design.    ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "KEcL0AFXVchEidIFBDkBW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 14090.381731728388,
      "y": -963.3557977003263,
      "width": 556.7796630859375,
      "height": 800,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bJR",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 493240182,
      "version": 1281,
      "versionNonce": 687593898,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1752198002969,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Database Schema\n\n- User\n    - id\n    - email\n    - phoneno\n    - createdtime\n    - updatedtime\n    ...\n\n- UserProfile\n    - id\n    - userId\n    - profiletype // DRIVER , RIDER\n    - value: { payload contain details about vehicle etc. }\n\nDriverAvailabilty\n    - id\n    - userprofileId\n    - isavailable.\n\n- Ride\n    - id\n    - source\n    - destination\n    - created time\n    - status // START , INPRGRESS, FAILED, SUCCESS\n    - updatedtime\n    - vehiclecategoryId.  // different type of vehicle\n \n    \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Database Schema\n\n- User\n    - id\n    - email\n    - phoneno\n    - createdtime\n    - updatedtime\n    ...\n\n- UserProfile\n    - id\n    - userId\n    - profiletype // DRIVER , RIDER\n    - value: { payload contain details about vehicle etc. }\n\nDriverAvailabilty\n    - id\n    - userprofileId\n    - isavailable.\n\n- Ride\n    - id\n    - source\n    - destination\n    - created time\n    - status // START , INPRGRESS, FAILED, SUCCESS\n    - updatedtime\n    - vehiclecategoryId.  // different type of vehicle\n \n    \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
