    {
      "id": "XD3g7y1UZAfgWjnJ2GL2e",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 15953.58388246427,
      "y": 419.22718412150766,
      "width": 798.5394897460938,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bMI",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 378285802,
      "version": 676,
      "versionNonce": 245773866,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "vJYG8or_yezZNNNespBXB",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1752199651226,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "multiple solution.\n1. db lock + update status not available + also maintain \n   timeout, unlock can be delayed in case of server crash , because in memory lock.\n2. maintain driver id whihc need to be locked in redis\n    with ttl. So while check for other, first check this.\n    we'll have to do track off with reliabilty for timeout 10 second. \n    rare possibility of problem\n    \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "multiple solution.\n1. db lock + update status not available + also maintain \n   timeout, unlock can be delayed in case of server crash , because in memory lock.\n2. maintain driver id whihc need to be locked in redis\n    with ttl. So while check for other, first check this.\n    we'll have to do track off with reliabilty for timeout 10 second. \n    rare possibility of problem\n    \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "A9syArA_cgh2ny2h_XUZj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 15674.96215072398,
      "y": 1336.6135424942536,
      "width": 1547.4190673828125,
      "height": 420,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bMJ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 926439210,
      "version": 651,
      "versionNonce": 54099242,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "cKkE0-ZYsHL8WEaRb7tvX",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1752199615584,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Challenges:\n1. location updation -> redis\n2. High frequency update from user ( can make some algo that will as per activity update period like instead of 5\n    second , can be more second if stable or off the mobile )\n2. driver locking -> redis\n3. too much ride request -> matching service\n    take some time how to scale this \n4. at matching server, what if driver deny\n    how to send to new driver or how to solve this.\n    - \n5. more low latency -> geo sharding logically for all thing\n    - managing problem.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Challenges:\n1. location updation -> redis\n2. High frequency update from user ( can make some algo that will as per activity update period like instead of 5\n    second , can be more second if stable or off the mobile )\n2. driver locking -> redis\n3. too much ride request -> matching service\n    take some time how to scale this \n4. at matching server, what if driver deny\n    how to send to new driver or how to solve this.\n    - \n5. more low latency -> geo sharding logically for all thing\n    - managing problem.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
